1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,530
A story from the household of the Prophet.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,620
How ‘A’ishah performed ruqyah for the Prophet (peace be upon him)

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,950
‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said:

4
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:11,650
When the Prophet (peace be upon him) fell ill, he would recite the Mu‘awwidhat over himself,

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,570
and blow lightly.

6
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:14,120
When his pain grew severe,

7
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:17,450
‘A’ishah would sit by him and recite them over him,

8
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:20,390
and wipe him with his own hand, hoping for its blessing.

9
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:22,470
This is the Prophet of Allah —

10
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,680
the one with the greatest trust in Allah of all creation — turning to the Qur’an in illness.

11
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:30,610
He recited over himself first, and his wife recited over him when the pain intensified.

12
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:33,670
So you do not need a sheikh or a famous reciter.

13
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,710
Start with yourself and your family,

14
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:39,020
as the Prophet (peace be upon him) and his family did.

15
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,560
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

